  "title": "Miller-2019-library-10.1038/s41562-019-0678-3",
  "description": "A BIDS-formatted subset of Kai Miller's library of human electrocorticographic (ECoG) data, comprising 111 recordings from 24 epilepsy patients with subdural electrode grids. It covers six calibrated tasks: finger flexion, hand gestures, motor imagery, basic motor movement, and speech tasks (verb generation and noun reading). Recordings were made at 1 kHz with Synamps2 amplifiers and converted to BrainVision format with events and electrode positions.",
  "methods_description": "Subdural ECoG was recorded at Harborview Hospital in Seattle with Synamps2 amplifiers at 1000 Hz, using BCI2000 and a built-in 0.15-200 Hz band pass. Patients performed cued movement, imagery, gesture and speech tasks. MATLAB source files were converted to BrainVision with MNE-BIDS and scaled to physical units, with no filtering, resampling or re-referencing.",
